:: StoryTitle
Curse of the Silent House


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "5F7696DB-6CCB-4228-B230-3052727166A8",
  "format": "Brass Basilisk",
  "format-version": "0.1.3",
  "start": "BACKGROUND",
  "zoom": 1
}


:: 1 {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
You stand in the shadow of the looming, unsettling house. Beside the heavy, ancient door hangs a thick, faded bell rope.

If you knock upon the door, turn to 2.
If you pull the bell rope, turn to 3.
If you boldly try to open the  door, turn to 4.


:: 10 {"position":"700,650","size":"100,100"}
You throw yourself to the side, desperately dodging past the snapping jaws of the beast. Its teeth miss your flesh, but its razor-sharp claws rake across your arm, leaving a deep, bleeding gash.

Your VIGOUR decreases by 2.

The giant rat hisses and melts back into the darkness. Shaking off the encounter, you press cautiously down the hall. Turn to 12.


:: 11 {"position":"825,650","size":"100,100"}
The monstrous rat gives one final twitch, rolls onto its back, and lies still. You straighten up and flourish your sword, both to celebrate your hard-won victory and to flick the foul black blood from the steel. But as you slide it back into its scabbard, a bizarre sight stops you cold: the rat's carcass dissolves into the shadows, vanishing completely.

Shaking your head in sheer puzzlement, you turn and proceed down the shadowy hall. Turn to 12.


:: 12 {"position":"575,850","size":"100,100"}
You walk cautiously down the seemingly endless corridor, every sense on high alert. But as you advance, a subtle change creeps into the very air. The temperature drops, and an unnatural calm descends upon the hall. The dim, diffuse light takes on a strange, mellow haze that dances at the edges of your vision. A heavy, sweet lethargy seeps into your bones, clouding your mind... an overwhelming drowsiness is pulling you down...

Roll one die, and try to roll less than or equal to your current PSI. If you succeed, turn to 14. If you fail, turn to 13.


:: 13 {"position":"800,825","size":"100,100"}
Your legs give way and you slump against the wall, eventually sliding down to lie upon the cold floor.

The lethargy wraps around you like a heavy, suffocating blanket. Every movement feels like a monumental chore, and soon, even the simplest tasks seem entirely pointless. Including the effort to...draw...breath...

You are dead.



:: 14 {"position":"575,975","size":"100,100"}
You recognise the insidious touch of a psychic compulsion—an unseen mind or ancient spell is trying to lull you into an eternal slumber.

Gritting your teeth, you marshal your mental strength and push back against the magical fog. The heavy lethargy shatters, and your mind snaps back into sharp, crystal clarity. You are wide awake and ready for whatever lies ahead.

Turn to 15.



:: 15 {"position":"700,1025","size":"100,100"}
And now it is up to you to tell the rest of the story.



:: 2 {"position":"475,25","size":"100,100"}
You pound your fist against the heavy wood. The dull, booming thud tells you the door is incredibly solid. You knock repeatedly, but only silence greets you. Your knuckles throb painfully from the impact.

Your VIGOUR decreases by 2.

Will you now pull the faded bell rope (turn to 3), or try to push the door open (turn to 4)?


:: 3 {"position":"400,300","size":"100,100"}
A deep, resonant gong echoes from somewhere deep within the house. After a tense, silent pause, the heavy door slowly swings inward with a long, ominous creak.

Turn to 7.


:: 4 {"position":"575,175","size":"100,100"}
You push against the heavy wood, but the door refuses to budge. It is firmly locked. You may, of course, step back and pull the faded bell rope (turn to 3). Alternatively, you can try your luck at picking the lock.

Roll one die. If you roll 1 to 3, turn to 5. If you roll 4 to 6, turn to 6.


:: 5 {"position":"550,300","size":"100,100"}
You fumble with the lock, but your tools slip uselessly against the mechanism. Cursing your luck, you step back and yank the bell rope in frustration.

Turn to 3.


:: 6 {"position":"700,300","size":"100,100"}
Your nimble fingers find the tumblers with ease. With a satisfying click, the mechanism gives way, and the heavy door swings inward with a long, ominous creak.

Turn to 7.


:: 7 {"position":"500,500","size":"100,100"}
No sooner have you stepped across the threshold than the heavy door slams shut behind you with a resounding crash! You pull and push at the handle, but the unyielding wood refuses to budge. Trapped inside, there is nothing for it but to press deeper into the house.

You peer into the gloom and realize you are standing in a vast, echoing hall. Faint, grey light filtering from the outside illuminates the dusty, bare floorboards immediately around the entrance. Beyond that small pool of light, the rest of the great hall is swallowed by musty, impenetrable darkness.

Then, a dry, chittering sound echoes from the shadows. Out of the blackness, a pair of malevolent red eyes locks onto you.

Turn to 8.


:: 8 {"position":"700,525","size":"100,100"}
Your sword leaps into your hand as if by magic! Your heart pounds with a mix of dread and excitement as a monstrous rat, easily the size of a wild boar, scuttles out from the shadows. Its eyes are fevered and bloodshot, its yellow teeth are bared, and thick, foul-smelling froth drips from its jaws.

RAT VIGOUR 9

Roll two dice:
score 02 to 03  the rat bites your neck; lose 30 VIGOUR
score 04 to 06  the rat hits you and you lose 3 VIGOUR
score 07 to 11  the rat is hit and loses 3 VIGOUR
score 12 to 12 you strike a killing blow, and the rat loses 9 VIGOUR

If you win, turn to 11. If you lose, turn to 9. If you FLEE, turn to 10.


:: 9 {"position":"575,650","size":"100,100"}
The monstrous rat lunges, its filthy teeth tearing into your jugular. Your vision fades to black as you feel the utter terror of the giant rodent draining the very life from your veins.

You are dead.


:: BACKGROUND {"position":"100,100","size":"100,100"}
Far beyond the city limits, where the windswept moors give way to the creeping shadows of the ancient forest—or perhaps just a little way inside it—stands a solitary house. No one knows who built it, nor when. No one can recall a single soul ever calling it home. The relentless woods have not reclaimed it, its timbers have not rotted, and its secrets remain locked within. Yet, it is a mystery that haunts the minds of all who know of it.

Over the years, wild rumours have swirled around the dwelling. Tavern tales speak of hoarded treasure, of grand halls draped in rich tapestries and illuminated by gleaming crystal chandeliers. Locals whisper of phantom voices, eerie lights flickering in the dead of night, and foolish adventurers who crossed the threshold and never returned. It is this final rumour that chills the blood of even the bravest.

It has taken years of hard training, but you have finally honed your skills and gathered your resolve to brave the house. With a well-stocked pack on your back and your trusty sword at your hip, you set out. The journey is long and arduous. As the sun dips below the western horizon, casting long, skeletal shadows through the trees, you finally reach the forest's edge. The house looms before you, silent and waiting.

NOW TURN TO 1.
